{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 310,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the last video, I introduced the idea that\nreally small things act sometimes like waves,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4770,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and sometimes like particles."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6450,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how can we actually picture the wave-particle\nduality of, say, an electron?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 11050,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, imagine our electron is a speck of dust\nin a raindrop."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14650,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We know pretty well where the speck is, at\nfirst."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17130,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when the drop hits the ground, it'll spread\nout like a wave - and the speck of dust will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20880,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be somewhere in that wave."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22880,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So the speck (our electron) is guided by the\nwave - but there's still only one speck, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27740,
    "dDurationMs": 2890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if you actually look for it, you'll only find\nit in one place."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30630,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The wave will also tell you how likely you\nare to find the speck at any one point – if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34990,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the drop splits in two, you're more likely\nto find the speck wherever there's more water!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39490,
    "dDurationMs": 3610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's pretty much how the wave-particle\nduality of quantum mechanics works: each particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43100,
    "dDurationMs": 5890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is guided by a wave that determines the chances\nit'll be in a certain place or state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48990,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Easy, right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49990,
    "dDurationMs": 12200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The hard part is figuring out the movement\nof the waves!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
